# Blacklist for backup.sh: things that are NOT copied.
#
# One rsync exclude pattern per line; "#" starts a comment line. Trailing
# comments are NOT supported: the whole line is the pattern.
# A leading "/" anchors the pattern to the top of the source folder, a trailing
# "/" only matches folders, "*" is a wildcard. Without a "/" the pattern matches
# that name at any depth.
#
# This list wins over backup.allow and is applied first, which has two
# consequences worth remembering:
#   - a folder excluded here is never entered, so nothing inside it can be
#     allowed back in. That is why "/Library/" is NOT in this file: ~/Library
#     is a keep-only area defined in backup.allow.
#   - it is the only way to trim the copy in ~ of a folder that backup.allow
#     allows at any depth (.vscode/, .cursor/, .codex/, .cargo/).
#
# Hidden files and folders (names starting with ".") are skipped anyway unless
# backup.allow lists them, so they only need an entry here to override an allow
# entry. The hidden entries below are kept as documentation of intent.
#
# Tweak this file using extensions.csv in the run's folder under logs/: anything
# in there that you don't want, add it here (e.g. "*.log"), then run the script
# again.
# Files that were already copied stay in the backup, since nothing is deleted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extensions that are not worth recovering
#
# Only add extensions that are known to be machine-generated: leaving out a file
# someone made is worse than carrying a little extra data. Deliberately NOT
# listed, because they can hold authored or costly-to-redo data:
#   *.bundle     a git bundle is a portable repository, made on purpose
#   *.pkl        pickled data and models
#   *.opf        ebook metadata
#   *.xcsettings Xcode project settings
# Check an extension against extensions.csv before adding it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.agent
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
*.hbc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient lock and runtime files.
# NOT "*.lock": that would throw away yarn.lock, Cargo.lock, Gemfile.lock,
# poetry.lock and friends, which are worth keeping to rebuild a project.
# There is no "*.db" either: SQLite files hold real user data (Messages,
# Notes, browser profiles). Exclude a disposable database by its path instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pid
*.pid.lock
.~lock.*#
/.gnupg/*.lock
/.gnupg/S.gpg-agent*
/.ssh/*.sock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated files and editor leftovers
# ("*.bak" and "*.backup" are deliberately absent: they are often hand-made.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
~$*
*.orig
*.rej
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.class
*.o
*.obj

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable build output and dependency folders, anywhere in the tree.
# "build", "dist" and "target" are a deliberate tradeoff: they are nearly
# always generated, but a hand-written folder with that name would be lost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
__pycache__/
venv/
Pods/
build/
dist/
target/
coverage/
DerivedData/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hidden caches and generated folders. The allow list would skip these anyway;
# they are listed so the intent is on paper and stays that way if a future
# allow entry would otherwise let them in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.next/
.nuxt/
.turbo/
.parcel-cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.localized
/.CFUserTextEncoding

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Top-level folders in ~
# ~/Library is NOT here on purpose; see the header and backup.allow.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App bundles and app data (reinstall / re-sync instead)
/Applications/
/Applications (Parallels)/
# Virtual machines (very large), remove this line to keep them
/Parallels/
# Empty mount points for network drives
/Drives/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hidden folders that backup.allow allows at any depth (for projects), trimmed
# down to the parts worth keeping for the copy directly in ~.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# installed extensions
/.vscode/
/.cursor/extensions/
# downloaded plugins and scratch data
/.codex/plugins/
/.codex/computer-use/
/.codex/dictation-history/
# downloaded crates and build cache
/.cargo/registry/
/.cargo/git/
/.cargo/bin/
# Yarn's global package cache
/.yarn/berry/cache/
/.yarn/cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trimmings inside folders that backup.allow keeps whole
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.docker/desktop-build/
/.docker/run/
# credential and API caches, plugin downloads: recreated by `aws sso login`,
# kubectl, terraform init and pulumi
/.aws/cli/cache/
/.aws/sso/cache/
/.kube/cache/
/.kube/http-cache/
/.terraform.d/plugin-cache/
/.pulumi/plugins/
/.local/share/Trash/
/.config/*/Cache/
/.config/*/CachedData/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~/.ssh: keep keys and config, skip what ssh recreates itself
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.ssh/known_hosts*
/.ssh/agent/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~/Library trimmings: the keep-only areas in backup.allow still contain
# caches and per-workspace state that is rebuilt on first launch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Library/Application Support/Code/User/History/
/Library/Application Support/Code/User/workspaceStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Code/User/globalStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Code - Insiders/User/History/
/Library/Application Support/Code - Insiders/User/workspaceStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Code - Insiders/User/globalStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Cursor/User/History/
/Library/Application Support/Cursor/User/workspaceStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Cursor/User/globalStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/History/
/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/workspaceStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/globalStorage/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/BrowserMetrics/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/component_crx_cache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/extensions_crx_cache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/Cache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/Code Cache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/GPUCache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/DawnGraphiteCache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/DawnWebGPUCache/
/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/*/Service Worker/
/Library/Application Support/JetBrains/*/caches/
/Library/Application Support/JetBrains/*/log/
/Library/Application Support/JetBrains/*/index/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Worth reviewing for your own setup
#   - build/, dist/ and target/ are excluded at any depth. That is nearly always
#     right, but a hand-written folder with one of those names would be skipped.
#   - ~/Library/Containers and Group Containers hold app data for sandboxed
#     apps. Only what backup.allow names is kept.
#   - .idea/ is kept whole; trim it if it turns out to be mostly machine state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
